<title>LEBANON: Yields mixed on Lebanese t-bills.</title>
<headline>Yields mixed on Lebanese t-bills.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Lebanon shaved a single point off yields on three-and six-month treasury bills on Monday but kept one- and two-year yields unchanged for the fifth successive week.</p>
<p>The Bank announced the following interest rates for its April 17 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.26 (13.27)	     13.71 (13.72)</p>
<p>    Six months	    13.48 (13.49)	     14.45 (14.46)</p>
<p>    12 months	     13.20 (13.20)	     15.20 (15.20)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 16.08 (16.08)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308</p>
